{"id": "DeJyswKCtCY", "title": "Video by kodekloud", "description": "Shift Left Security, Explained!\ud83d\udc1b\n\nShift left is the practice of moving security checks earlier in the software delivery line so issues get caught before code reaches production. SAST (static application security testing) scans code without running it, like CodeQL in a CI pipeline. DAST (dynamic application security testing) attacks the running app from outside, like OWASP ZAP in staging. Pre-commit hooks run a quick scanner like Semgrep on changed files before code enters Git, and editor plugins like SonarQube flag problems as code is written.\n\nThe example used is SQL injection, where input like ' OR 1=1 -- ends up inside the query and returns every order in the table. The fix is a parameterized query, so user input is always treated as plain data.\n\nWhich of these checks does your pipeline actually run? Comment below.\n\n#ShiftLeft #DevSecOps #SAST #DAST #SQLInjection #DevOps #AppSec #CodeQL #OWASPZAP #Semgrep #SonarQube #PreCommit #CICD #KodeKloud #Shorts", "channel": "kodekloud", "uploader_id": "23282220284", "uploader": "KodeKloud | DevOps Learning Platform", "timestamp": 1791290094, "like_count": 8040, "comment_count": 35, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-18132621421780285a", "manifest_url": null, "ext": "m4a", "width": null, "height": null, "tbr": 57.328, "asr": 48000, "fps": null, "language": null, "format_note": "DASH audio", "filesize": null, "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "dynamic_range": null, "url": "https://scontent-sjc6-1.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOjoX9jlsWSaCw5W_IJRbcalxY9iZtU7GtcmwiV6bBmsbLRDQMUkXE5K