": "11", "resolution": "1080x1080"}, {"url": "https://scontent-sjc6-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/839490337_18132621700780285_3952655300534037718_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=100&ig_cache_key=NDAwMTk1MjcyMTU4NjAxNjQwODE4MTMyNjIxNjk3NzgwMjg1.3-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=58cdad&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNMSVBTLnhwaWRzLjExNTIuc2RyLnZpZGVvX2RlZmF1bHRfY292ZXJfZnJhbWUuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=OkB_8UVX83MQ7kNvwH72O7B&_nc_oc=Ado3DMwsmkfp0FvCNDai_L0HDmEnsNZnjVFFpqZGAG1XK7Hv5Ej7oX5hUbXHfLRKnm4&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-sjc6-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=xkhHCsxfkn1CsluVVh2iYw&_nc_ss=79689&oh=00_AQO5pABExB4hEMgYYCkLPfLsIbWshlcuYDm3iudT9eRfeg&oe=6AE60E76", "width": 1152, "height": 2048, "id": "12", "resolution": "1152x2048"}], "comments": [{"author": "why_vt", "author_id": "10478134550", "id": "18106043450355755", "text": "Why can't you just validate the input before using it in a sql query?? If it's not a number or string of numbers then don't go further with it.", "timestamp": 1793034307, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "ema.fab75", "author_id": "53645827431", "id": "18129187844306401", "text": "So, someone invented a term, \"shift left\", for something that is expected since last century?", "timestamp": 1792659499, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "adrianmnh", "author_id": "283157989", "id": "18119880439755778", "text": "Seeequilllllll", "timestamp": 1792248578, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "tope_bravura", "author_id": "1098229198", "id": "18386111230230336", "text": "Nice!", "timestamp": 1791800331, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "serversmatter", "author_id": "35156473083", "id": "17927736909423028", "text": "semgrep pre-commit plus codeql in ci, dast never made it out of staging for us", "timestamp": 1791517529, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "bendrape", "author_id": "68850773261", "id": "17984675217094258", "text": "Taking notes. Thanks", "timestamp": 1791413145, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "mmedhat_19", "author_id": "1704228872", "id": "18075070844459415", "text": "Thank you for giving the whole advice without  saying \"if you want bla bla, write bla bla in comments\".", "timestamp": 1791360243, "like_count": 12}, {"author": "ohislawrence", "author_id": "2091744677", "id": "17898387417606652", "text": "Well, I don't really have to worry about this with a framework like laraval", "timestamp": 1791359640, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "dannyelias751", "author_id": "65977333661", "id": "17888724492653893", "text": "\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udd25nicee", "timestamp": 1791345232, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "damvepo", "author_id": "11143350613", "id": "18007723667989958", "text": "If you implement SAST, SCA, DAST, container scanning, infraestructure security with checkov for example, what else can you protect as a devops?", "timestamp": 1791344038, "like_count": 6}, {"author": "fh.montibeller", "author_id": "73756015979", "id": "18137447974553331", "text": "Shift left? It's rollback", "timestamp": 1791331176, "like_count": 2}, {"author": "tory_loop", "author_id": "7751311629", "id": "18060307778537020", "text": "Good thing ORMs fixed this a long time ago\ud83d\udc40", "timestamp": 1791323222, "like_count": 7}, {"author": "suhail_kaka", "author_id": "1359073039", "id": "18151254475539226", "text": "Embedding quality engineering principles early on in the development lifecycle, prior to the code being written, could detect such anomalies earlier. I'm perplexed that testing was entirely omitted from this flow @kodekloud", "timestamp": 1791314218, "like_count": 7}], "webpage_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeJyswKCtCY/", "original_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeJyswKCtCY/", "webpage_url_basename": "DeJyswKCtCY", "webpage_url_domain": "instagram.com", "extractor": "Instagram", "extractor_key": "Instagram", "playlist": null, "playlist_index": null, "thumbnail": "https://scontent-sjc6-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/839490337_18132621700780285_3952655300534037718_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=100&ig_cache_key=NDAwMTk1